WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.679 --> 00:00:03.990 align:start position:0%
 
this  is all that's left of the bus after the  powerful explosion in a kabul suburb  the bus was carrying soldiers home when  the suicide bomber struck  hardly a day goes by when the afghan  capital is spared attack  just hours earlier at least 12 soldiers  were shot dead by taliban gunmen  while they were working to clear mines  in helmand province  the violence came on the same day that  germany's defense minister ozola  fondelion  made an unannounced visit to the  bundesberg's base in mazari sharif  the bundeswehr mission with the most  casualties in the german military's  post-war history  ends in three weeks  fund alliance said germany owed it to  the victims to continue helping afghan  forces boost their security capabilities  the taliban will stop at nothing to  destabilize the fragile new government  in this transitional phase  that means it's all the more important  for us to stand alongside afghan  security forces and help them  counter this threat afghanistan  about 850 german troops are set to  remain in afghanistan  to help train and advise afghan soldiers  as part of what's being called mission  resolute support

